      "title": "Prompt-cache amplification by account (cache-read \u00d7 non-cached input)",
      "description": "Cache-read tokens per non-cached input token per account (cache_read / clamp_min(input,1)). Prompt caching is doing enormous work fleet-wide \u2014 cache reads outnumber fresh input tokens by hundreds to one \u2014 so the informative signal is the AMPLIFICATION factor, not a share (which pins to ~100% for everyone and hides the variance). A higher factor = each fresh token of context is reused across far more cached requests = cheaper, faster. A conspicuously LOW factor on a high-throughput account is a prompt-caching opportunity (short-lived caches, cache-busting prompt churn). clamp_min the denominator to 1 so an idle account reads 0, not NaN.",
